    {
      "extracted_at": "2026-07-21T03:28:55Z",
      "payload": {
        "chunks": [
          {
            "attributes": {
              "earnings_from_operations_fy2021_usd": 11975000000,
              "revenue_fy2021_usd": 222899000000,
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "segment",
            "content": "UnitedHealthcare includes the combined results of operations of UnitedHealthcare Employer & Individual, UnitedHealthcare Medicare & Retirement, UnitedHealthcare Community & State and UnitedHealthcare Global. The U.S. businesses share significant common assets, including a contracted network of physicians, health care professionals, hospitals and other facilities, information technology and consumer engagement infrastructure and other resources.",
            "entity_name": "UNH UnitedHealthcare Segment",
            "entity_type_entity": "RevenueSegment",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "earnings_from_operations_fy2021_usd": 4462000000,
              "revenue_fy2021_usd": 54065000000,
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "segment",
            "content": "Optum Health focuses on care delivery, care management, wellness and consumer engagement, and health financial services. Optum Health is building a comprehensive, connected health care delivery and engagement platform by directly providing high-quality care, helping people manage chronic and complex health needs, and proactively engaging consumers in managing their health through in-person, in-home, virtual and digital clinical platforms.",
            "entity_name": "UNH Optum Health Segment",
            "entity_type_entity": "RevenueSegment",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "earnings_from_operations_fy2021_usd": 3398000000,
              "revenue_fy2021_usd": 12199000000,
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "segment",
            "content": "Optum Insight brings together advanced analytics, technology and health care expertise to deliver integrated services and solutions. Hospital systems, physicians, health plans, governments, life sciences companies and other organizations comprising the health care industry depend on Optum Insight to help them improve performance, achieve efficiency, reduce costs, meet compliance mandates and modernize their core operating systems to meet the changing needs of the health system.",
            "entity_name": "UNH Optum Insight Segment",
            "entity_type_entity": "RevenueSegment",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "earnings_from_operations_fy2021_usd": 4135000000,
              "revenue_fy2021_usd": 91314000000,
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "segment",
            "content": "Optum Rx offers pharmacy care services and programs, including retail network contracting, home delivery, specialty and community health pharmacy services, purchasing and clinical capabilities, and develops programs in areas such as step therapy, formulary management, drug adherence and disease/drug therapy management. Optum Rx integrates pharmacy and medical care and is positioned to serve patients with complex clinical needs and consumers looking for a better digital pharmacy experience with transparent pricing.",
            "entity_name": "UNH Optum Rx Segment",
            "entity_type_entity": "RevenueSegment",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "capital_return",
            "content": "Under its Board of Directors' authorization, the Company maintains a share repurchase program. The objectives of the share repurchase program are to optimize the Company's capital structure and cost of capital, thereby improving returns to shareholders, as well as to offset the dilutive impact of share-based awards. In June 2018, the Board renewed the Company's share repurchase program with an authorization to repurchase up to 100 million shares of its common stock.",
            "entity_name": "UNH FY2021 Share Repurchases",
            "entity_type_entity": "CapitalReturn",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "capital_return",
            "content": "In June 2021, the Company's Board of Directors increased the Company's quarterly cash dividend to shareholders to an annual rate of $5.80 compared to $5.00 per share, which the Company had paid since June 2020. Declaration and payment of future quarterly dividends is at the discretion of the Board and may be adjusted as business needs or market conditions change.",
            "entity_name": "UNH June 2021 Dividend Increase",
            "entity_type_entity": "CapitalReturn",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "material_event",
            "content": "In 2021, we entered into agreements to acquire multiple companies in the health care sector, most notably, Change Healthcare (NASDAQ: CHNG), subject to regulatory approval and other customary closing conditions. Additionally, in January 2022, we entered into agreements to acquire multiple companies in the health care sector, subject to regulatory approval and other customary closing conditions. The total anticipated capital required for these acquisitions, excluding the payoff of acquired indebtedness, is approximately $12 billion.",
            "entity_name": "UNH Pending Acquisition of Change Healthcare",
            "entity_type_entity": "MaterialEvent",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "legal_proceeding",
            "content": "On February 14, 2017, the DOJ announced its decision to pursue certain claims within a lawsuit initially asserted against the Company and filed under seal by a whistleblower in 2011. The whistleblower's complaint, which was unsealed on February 15, 2017, alleges the Company made improper risk adjustment submissions and violated the False Claims Act. In March 2019, the court denied the government's motion for partial summary judgment and dismissed the Company's counterclaims without prejudice. The Company cannot reasonably estimate the outcome which may result from this matter given its procedural status.",
            "entity_name": "DOJ False Claims Act Lawsuit vs. UnitedHealth Group",
            "entity_type_entity": "LegalProceeding",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "legal_proceeding",
            "content": "CMS has selected certain of the Company's local plans for risk adjustment data validation (RADV) audits to validate the coding practices of and supporting documentation maintained by health care providers and such audits may result in retrospective adjustments to payments made to the Company's health plans.",
            "entity_name": "CMS RADV Audits of UNH Local Health Plans",
            "entity_type_entity": "LegalProceeding",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "capital_structure_event",
            "content": "The Company has $5.6 billion five-year, $5.6 billion three-year and $3.8 billion 364-day revolving bank credit facilities with 24 banks, which mature in December 2026, December 2024 and December 2022, respectively. These facilities provide full liquidity support for the Company's commercial paper program and are available for general corporate purposes. As of December 31, 2021, no amounts had been drawn on any of the bank credit facilities.",
            "entity_name": "UNH Revolving Credit Facilities (December 2021)",
            "entity_type_entity": "CapitalStructureEvent",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          }
        ],
